# RaptorJudge — line-ending policy.
#
# Windows checkouts default to core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites text files to
# CRLF. That breaks the container entrypoints: `backend/entrypoint.sh` line 28
# is `set -eu`, and Alpine's BusyBox ash parses the trailing CR as an option,
# aborting the bootstrap with `line 28: illegal option -` (CRLF also breaks the
# executable-bit-less `sh ./script.sh` invocations and nginx config parsing).
# Force LF everywhere text is involved, whatever the platform's git config says.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
